title: Configuration
kind: overview
aliases: config
summary: All user configuration is one git repository under ~/.config/metafolder/, updated by merging the shipped defaults into your edits.

Everything you can configure — the daemon's and the CLI's settings, the GUI's
settings, keybindings, style, panel types and user commands, the query grammar,
the ignore presets ([[Ignore presets]]), the shipped scripts, even this documentation — lives in one
place, `~/.config/metafolder/`, and that place is a ''git repository''. The
shipped defaults sit on a `default` branch, your configuration on `main`, and an
update is a git merge of one into the other: your edits survive upgrades, even of
a file you changed, and a file you never touched follows the shipped one.

A missing or malformed file is an error, never a silent fallback to a built-in
default ([[No runtime fallback]]).

